-- Conformance: binding a reserved prelude-namespace type name is a checker error (Chapter 8, Section 8.4.1)
-- Tests: E154 — a type PARAMETER in the prelude's reserved `Vera` namespace is
-- rejected where it is bound (#1221 review).  A `forall` variable is neither a
-- declaration nor a reference: it BINDS the name for one declaration's body,
-- and type-parameter scope is consulted before either other rail, so a binder
-- here made every mention inside this function resolve to the type variable
-- while code generation resolved the same spelling to the prelude's own
-- declaration.  The reservation is closed at the binder too.
public forall<VeraOptionMapFn> fn pick(@VeraOptionMapFn -> @Int)
  requires(true)
  ensures(true)
  effects(pure)
{
  1
}
